A||||24||Her86GT||Who has a front plate???||||5||
Z||000000||Her86GT||09-29-2001||04:13 PM||||So, how many Fiero owners out there actually have their front plate on thier car?  I just got my first warning the other day for not having mine on the car.  Cop said it would be a $110 fine but said he wasn't having a bad day so I got off.  What's your story?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar2sm.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-29-2001||05:40 PM||||No front plate since I turned 16. 5 years later, and never once been given a problem about it(front plates are required in Ohio).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||09-29-2001||06:51 PM||||Jersey cops are a pain, gotta have the front plate.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero5||09-29-2001||08:11 PM||||Check out this thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009414.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009414.html</A> <P>Currently I am still running with my plate in my windshield. I refuse to put it on my front areo nose due to the poor wording of the law here in NH. I have the front plate on my other non aero nose models, but not on my Fiero9. The cops have apparently decided to leave me alone. It's been months with no incidents. They even dropped all charges against our son, and called and mailed us paperwork stating that the cases were dismissed.<P>I fought the law and I won  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Steve ||||reg||7
Z||000004||lowfierogt||09-30-2001||03:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Her86GT:<BR><B>So, how many Fiero owners out there actually have their front plate on thier car?  I just got my first warning the other day for not having mine on the car.  Cop said it would be a $110 fine but said he wasn't having a bad day so I got off.  What's your story?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I do.  After getting a ticket 5 years ago.  I paid a 75.00 fine.   Use the plate.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/87%20fiero_files/Jun0302.JPG">  <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||1
Z||000005||Svyn||09-30-2001||03:02 AM||||Just tell them, someone backed into you and your holder broke. Keep the plate inside the car and tell him you have one on order from GM, but its hard to find one. If he doesn't care after that bs speach you get off free, otherwise I think they can give you an inspection ticket (atleast in MD). ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||09-30-2001||03:07 AM||||Here in CA it is a requirement also. The worst that can happen to you is what we call a "Fix-it" ticket. <P>I wouldn't pay the money for a bracket though. If I got the ticket I would show up at the local station or doughnut shop and show them that I have the plate on the dash and get it written off.<P>P.S. It used to be "To serve and Protect"<BR>We've come to know it as "To observe and COLLECT"<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||Capt Fiero||09-30-2001||04:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>P.S. It used to be "To serve and Protect"<BR>We've come to know it as "To observe and COLLECT"<P>Sly[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I hear that, LOL.  But as for front plates, I ran around for a couple years getting warnings about it in BC, but I got ticketed for it about 12 months ago, so I made my own custom mount for it, so the plate lays almost flat against the lower part of the nose. (more like a 45 degree angle to the ground) The ticket I got was for like 180$ for having it in the windshield.  The other plate related ticket I got was 86$ for my lisc plate fram partially covering my year date tag on the bottom of my plate. I think the cops really do have a quota at the end of the month cause I always get the dumbest tickets right around the 28th of every month. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Her86GT||09-30-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B><BR>P.S. It used to be "To serve and Protect"<BR>We've come to know it as "To observe and COLLECT"<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is so true at times.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||x-thumpr-x||09-30-2001||09:41 PM||||Here in T.O. you get alot of crack downs on drivers with no front plates. One genius in the club came up with an Idea, he bought an easily removable bra for is GT, then had a leather puoch sown on the front for the plate. Now he can remove the plate at will, and for shows, he takes the whole bra off in 10 seconds!  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Brandon86SE||09-30-2001||09:44 PM||||Gotta love Alberta!  We don't have front plates here.  The first thing I did to my car when I got it was take off the front plate holder, it looked rather nasty.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
